{{Quote|You are a Mandalorian! Your ancestors rode the great Mythosaur.|Kuiil scolds Din Djarin|<ref name="Mando1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref>}}
'''Mythosaurs''' were creatures of gigantic proportions found on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Mandalore]]. The [[Mines of Mandalore]] were a mythosaur lair. They were allegedly tamed and ridden by [[Mandalore the Great]] and ancient [[Mandalorian]]s, but they were believed to have gone extinct long before the [[Annihilation|Mandalorian cataclysm]], although at least one mythosaur survived and lived in the [[Living Waters]] during the time of the [[New Republic]]. Its [[Bone|skull]] was one of the traditional symbols of Mandalorian iconography, and some [[Mandalorian armor]] bore the distinctive symbol.

==Biology and appearance==
Mythosaurs were [[Water|sea]] beasts<ref name="sw100">''[[Star Wars 100 Objects]]''</ref> of gigantic proportions;<ref name="BMF32" /> they could grow to be more than 30 [[meter]]s (100 feet) in length.<ref name="SWECG" /> Mythosaurs had [[Color|yellowish]] scaly skin with black eyes and bore two large horns on the side of their mouth. They could survive both on land and [[Water|underwater]].<ref name="Chapter 18" /> Mythosaurs used their sharp tusks to fight competitors or possibly to catch prey. There are many questions regarding the biology of the mythosaur: was it lumbering as the apex predator in its environment, or was it fast and agile?<ref name="sw100" />

==History==
===Early history===
{{Quote|According to ancient folklore, the mines were once a Mythosaur lair. Mandalore the Great is said to have tamed the mythical beast. It is from these legends that the skull signet was adopted and became the symbol of our planet.|Bo-Katan Kryze reading the description of the Living Waters to Din Djarin|<ref name="Chapter 18" />}}
[[File:MythosaurSkull-SW100Objects.png|thumb|left|200px|A stylized beskar mythosaur skull in the possession of the Tribe.]]
The mythosaurs were found on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Mandalore]],<ref name="BMF32" /> and had a lair in its [[mines of Mandalore|mines]].<ref name="Chapter 18" /> Legends tell that long before the [[Mandalorian]]s had established themselves on Mandalore, the mythosaurs ruled the planet. They were allegedly tamed<ref name="Squadrons">''[[Star Wars: Squadrons]]''</ref> and ridden<ref name="Mando1" /> by [[Mandalore the Great]]<ref name="Chapter 18" /> and ancient [[Mandalorian]]s.<ref name="Squadrons" /> Some stories claimed that the Mandalorians tamed the beasts, other tales suggested the even greater feat that the Mandalorians rode the beasts while they were wild and free.<ref name="sw100" /> Long before the [[Annihilation|Mandalorian cataclysm]], they were believed to have become extinct,<ref name="BMF32" /> though at least one mythosaur survived.<ref name="Chapter 18" />

Though considered extinct, its memory lived on in the mythosaur [[Bone|skull]] emblem,<ref name="BMF32" /> one of the traditional symbols of Mandalorian iconography,<ref name="My Rebel Sketchbook">''[[Sabine My Rebel Sketchbook]]''</ref> with some [[Mandalorian armor]] bearing the distinctive symbol.<ref name="FoD">''[[Forces of Destiny: Tales of Hope & Courage]]''</ref> The creature shared its name with the [[mythosaur axe]], a [[melee weapon]] used by the Mandalorians. [[Vera Beroya's mythosaur axe|One]] of these was owned by [[Vera Beroya]] and her [[Nam Beroya|father]].<ref name="FLT">''[[Friends Like These]]''</ref>

===Time of the New Republic===
{{Quote|The songs of eons past foretold of the mythosaur rising up to herald a new age of Mandalore.|The Armorer|<ref name="ROTM">{{BOBF|Chapter 5: Return of the Mandalorian}}</ref>}}
[[File:Mythosaur-S3GN.jpg|thumb|right|250px|The mythosaur in the waters of the mines of Mandalore]]
In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Mandalorian date">{{MandoDate}}</ref> the [[Ugnaught]] [[Kuiil]]<ref name="Kuiil">{{Databank|kuiil|Kuiil}}</ref> was training the Mandalorian [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] to ride [[blurrg]]s on<ref name="Mando1" /> the planet [[Arvala-7]]<ref name="Kuiil" /> and scolded him when he tried to give up, reminding him of the fact that his ancestors rode mythosaurs and that blurrgs were easier to ride.<ref name="Mando1" />

By the [[New Republic Era|reign]] of the [[New Republic]], [[songs of eons past]] in the Mandalorian culture foretold of the mythosaur rising up to herald a new age of the Mandalorian culture.<ref name="ROTM" /> Indeed, [[Lady]] [[Bo-Katan Kryze]] discovered one still alive in the [[Living Waters]] in the Mines of Mandalore beneath [[Sundari]]'s ruins while rescuing [[Din Djarin]] from drowning after he fell into its depths.<ref name="Chapter 18" /> Afterwards, she concealed the fact she had seen the mythosaur from Djarin.<ref name="Chapter 19">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 19: The Convert}}</ref> She later asked [[the Armorer]] to inlay the symbol of the mythosaur on her new [[pauldron]] instead of another [[Nite Owls|Nite Owl]]. When she told the Armorer that she had encountered the mythosaur,<ref name="Chapter 20">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 20: The Foundling}}</ref> the Armorer elected to view it as a noble vision,<ref name="Season Three Companion">{{InsiderCite|222|Star Wars: The Mandalorian Season Three Companion|''Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season Three Companion}}</ref> replying that those who walk the [[Way of the Mandalore|Way]] see many visions.<ref name="Chapter 20" />

However, she soon took Kryze's claim as evidence of the new age<ref name="Chapter 21">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 21: The Pirate}}</ref> foretold in songs.<ref name="ROTM" /> After the [[Conflict on Mandalore|reconquest]] of Mandalore from [[Gideon's Imperial remnant]], the Mythosaur remained alive, still living within the Living Waters.<ref name="Chapter 24">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 24: The Return}}</ref>

==Mythosaurs in the galaxy==
The Mines of Mandalore were once a mythosaur lair. Mandalore the Great is said to have tamed the mythical beast. By the time of the New Republic, they were considered extinct, but a mythosaur resided in the Living Waters beneath the Mines of Mandalore in the ruins of the [[Civic Center]] of Sundari.<ref name="Chapter 18" />

A mythosaur skull hung from one of the walls in [[Dok-Ondar]]'s [[Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities|Den of Antiquities]] in [[Black Spire Outpost]], [[Batuu]].<ref name="Galaxy'sEdge">{{GEAttr|Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities}}</ref> Meanwhile, [[Oga's Cantina]] began serving an [[alcohol]]ic drink known as "[[The Mythosaur]]" in a drink cup resembling the creature itself.<ref name="Oga">{{GEAttr|Oga's Cantina}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Mythosaurs were first identified in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in the [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 32|thirty-second]] issue of the magazine ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]''.<ref name="BMF32" /> They first appeared in "[[Chapter 18: The Mines of Mandalore]]".<ref name="Chapter 18" /> The [[species]] originates in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where they were created for the [[1982]] comic book [[Star Wars (1977) 69|''Star Wars'' (1977) 69]], which was written by [[David Michelinie]].<ref name="SW69">[[Star Wars (1977) 69|''Star Wars'' (1977) 69]]</ref>

